    "message": "fix(ingest): don't bind a default import to a member named default\n\nThe renamed-import fallback matched `binding.imported` against every parsed\nsymbol in the provider file. For `import run from \"./m\"`, `imported` is the\nliteral sentinel 'default' rather than an export name, so any provider member\nthat happens to be *called* `default` — a method, getter, or static — satisfied\nthe lookup and produced a confident (0.9) edge to the wrong member.\n\nGuard the fallback with the same `!== 'default'` exclusion already used when\nbuilding rename bindings. Named renamed imports, the case this PR exists to\nfix, are unaffected: they short-circuit through filePublicNames.\n\nExisting default-import coverage all used a named default export\n(`export default actualName`), which resolves before the fallback — hence the\ngreen suite.",
